gilbert gottfried was always known for  his scathing wits and willingness to  push boundaries and before he passed  away he gave the world one more taste of  his humor keep watching to find out  about gottfried's final tweet the  entertainment industry is still reeling  from the devastating death of legendary  comedian gilbert gottfried on april 12  2022 godfried was an iconic performer  and voice actor who worked on many big  projects throughout his lengthy career  perhaps the one characteristic that  defined his work more than any other was  a shrill high-pitched voice he would  often use it for exaggerated comedic  effect in film roles and drawing  stand-up sets beyond the quality of his  voice however gottfried was well  respected by many of his peers for his  razor sharp wits this particular skill  of his was memorialized online by the  likes of jason alexander and ben stiller  among many other well-known actors and  comedians when performing his material  gottfried liked to push people's buttons  and he would venture into crude  territory in many of his routines while  this approach was one of many reasons  why fans loved him it also cost him work  at times i have to respect anyone who  doesn't admire me as a performer  in one notable case he lost his gig  voicing the aflac duck after sharing  what many considered to be an  insensitive joke on twitter this never  dissuaded gottfried from leaning into  his particular brand of humor though as  evidenced by his final tweeted joke  where he appeared to throw a little  shade at none other than fellow comedian  chris rock on march 28th through his  official twitter account gottfried  posted a picture of himself and chris  rock the text accompanying the photo  seemed like it was poking fun at rock he  would only just been slapped by actor  will smith got freed asked which is the  worst crime chris roger being physically  assaulted or chris rock telling a joke  gottfried later posed the exact same  question to the associated press in an  interview but added that's it pure and  simple he made a joke this takes the  sting off the tweet a bit and makes it  clear that gottfried was defending his  friend but the tweet on its own could be  read as a jab jabber rock's dated gi  jane joke these types of humorous  provocations were gottfried's bread and  butter as a comedian the comic loved to  make light of what was being talked  about in the world from his own  idiosyncratic point of view in a  particularly edgy performance gottfried  told a joke about the 911 attacks only  weeks after they took place which led to  him being booed by the crowd furthermore  roasting other comedians and actors was  something for which gottfried was well  known for example he was a regular  participant in comedy central roast  specials often times delivering some of  the most laughed up bits of the night at  the expense of the celebrity guest it's  fitting then that gottfried's last joke  on twitter was one that so clearly  matched his particular brand of humor  commenting on current events and  roasting celebs responses to gilbert  gottfried's final tweet varied  significantly before and after news of  his death became public knowledge one  twitter user felt that will smith's slap  should be taken more seriously that  tweet was liked more than 100 times many  other replies from that same day contain  arguments about the significance of the  slab while humorous replies appear to be  few and far between compared to mostly  sincere responses following news of  gottfried's death however the tone  shifted with many twitter users sharing  his joke as a testament to his skill as  a comic  one user quote tweeted gottfried's quip  and added the caption brutal to the end  another shared gottfried's tweet and  wrote this gotta be the best last tweet  someone ever said  similarly another poster retweeted  gottfried's joke and added he's gone too  soon but at least he left twitter on a  high note in total gottfried's final  twitter joke was quote tweeted more than  350 times typically by users sharing it  in tribute to his sense of humor and the  fact that it endured into its final days  the tweet was also retweeted with no  accompanying texts more than  600 times and liked by more than 20 000  users given that much of this engagement  seems to have occurred not when it was  originally posted but following the news  of his passing this tweet now stands as  something of an online monument to the  late comic
 

